# Debugging with local-backend logs

## How it fits together
- `npm run dev` (repo root) builds `packages/shared` and `packages/pipeline`, then runs `tsc --watch` for both, **local-backend** (Fastify + tsx watch, http://localhost:8787) and **Vite** (http://localhost:5173). Vite proxies `/api/*` and `/ws` to the backend, so the browser never calls Google directly. The backend imports the packages from `dist/`, so rebuild them after editing.
- `npm run dev` does not build or watch `@krayon/api`. After editing `packages/api`, run `npm run build -w @krayon/api`.
- The backend mocks Google Cloud locally:
  - Firestore → SQLite at `local-backend/data/firestore.sqlite3` (table `docs`: collection, id, data JSON, updated)
  - Cloud Storage → files under `local-backend/data/storage/`
  - Auth → stub user `local-user` (override with the `X-User-Id` header)
  - Jobs → in-process (`course`, `resumeCourse`, `retryCourse`, `retryChapter`, `renderLesson`, `rerenderLesson`, `regenerate`), status in `jobs/{id}` docs
- Gemini is **real**: Vertex AI, project `krayon-ai`, location `global`, model `GEMINI_MODEL` (default `gemini-2.5-flash`) and `GEMINI_REVIEW_MODEL`, via gcloud Application Default Credentials (`GEMINI_API_KEY` is only a fallback). Config lives in `local-backend/.env`.

## Pipeline (`packages/pipeline/src/`)
Course → chapter → lesson → segment. `pipeline.ts` wires the stages; every step is stored as it finishes, so a restart resumes from the stored stage.
1. **Structure** (`chapters.ts`, call `structure`): the only call that attaches the whole PDF. Returns chapters with printed TOC pages and file pages; `pageRanges.ts` maps printed numbers to PDF indexes (`/PageLabels`, then running headers, then titles in the page text, then the model's samples) and snaps each start to its title. `normalizeRanges` then sorts, clamps, snaps overlaps, and closes gaps in code. The model is asked again only when there are no chapters or every chapter is skipped. Front and back matter are `skip`.
2. **Chapters** (`CHAPTER_CONCURRENCY` at once): `chapterText` per ≤30-page slice (halved on `MAX_TOKENS`), `lessonOutline` (pages clamped and sorted in code; only an empty outline is retried), one `lessonScript` per lesson (the prompt aims for 420–660 words; `scriptLength.ts` merges a lesson under half the minimum and splits one over 1.5× the maximum when both halves still meet the minimum), `studyDoc` (a cut-off last line is dropped; `withShorterRetry` retries once on `MAX_TOKENS` only). Lessons are stored `outlined`. Partial work (`chapterText`, `outline`, `drafts`, `planned`) lives on the chapter doc. A failed chapter marks its lessons that are still `writing` as `failed`, so Retry can rebuild them.
3. **Lesson render** (`lessonRender.ts`): only chapter 1 lesson 1 starts on its own; others start on `POST /api/lessons/:id/render`. `beats` splits the verbatim script by word count (`beats.ts`: split over 35 words, merge under 15; duration is the 6–15 s estimate). Then, when `TTS_ENABLED` is on, `voice` synthesizes one WAV per segment (cached; the lesson's own priority, so a clicked lesson jumps the TTS queue), and `retime` sets `durationInFrames` from the audio length plus a 0.6 s pause, capped at 60 s. Then per segment: `scene` (normalized, then validated; repair only for a structurally broken scene) → keyframes → `review` → fix. A segment gets `1 + SEGMENT_RETRIES` tries. The lesson is `ready` only when every segment is voiced (if TTS is on) and its scene is ready; otherwise `failed`. Retry re-runs failed segments and keeps audio that already exists. `TTS_ENABLED=false` skips voice and uses the 6–15 s estimate (silent video).
- Scene, review, script, and chat calls get page slices (`pdf.ts`), never the full file (`assertSliced` throws). Logs show `attached_pages`.
- Queues (`queue.ts`): one Gemini queue (`GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENCY`), one TTS queue (`TTS_CONCURRENCY`), and one render queue (`RENDER_CONCURRENCY`). Order: user-clicked lesson/chat first, then the viewed course (latest `/ws` subscribe), then auto lesson → chapter work → background, oldest first.
- Docs: `users/{uid}/courses/{c}/chapters/{ch}`, `…/lessons/{l}` (has `chapterId`), `…/lessons/{l}/segments/{s}/rounds/{n}`. Top-level indexes: `courseIndex/{c}`, `chapterIndex/{ch}`, `lessonIndex/{l}`, `courseViews/{c}`. Page text is a blob at `users/{uid}/pagetext/{sourceId}.json`. TTS cache is in-memory plus the audio blob `users/{uid}/audio/{hash}.wav`. Ids: `{courseId}-c1`, `{chapterId}-l1`, `s01`. Audio is served at `GET /api/audio/:blobId` (Range → 206).
- Retry, scoped to where it failed: `POST /api/courses/:id/retry` (structure), `POST /api/chapters/:id/retry`, `POST /api/lessons/:id/retry`. Learner rewrite: `POST /api/lessons/:id/segments/:sid/regenerate`. Chat: `POST /api/lessons/:id/ask` (`call_type=chat`).
- Restart recovery (`docstore.recoverInterrupted`): writing chapters → pending, rendering lessons → queued, unfinished segments → pending (ready ones are kept), a segment with `voice: voicing` → `pending`, then `resumeCourse` per open course.
- Reset everything: `curl -X POST localhost:8787/api/admin/reset` (local dev only; also the header's "Clear resources" button). It also clears the slice/page-text caches, TTS audio blobs, all three queues, and stops runs in flight.
- Tests: `npm test` (shared + pipeline + local-backend with `AI=0`). `npm run test:backend` (real Vertex calls).

## Schemas: one source of truth
- zod schemas in `packages/shared/src/schemas.ts` define every model response (`structure`, `chapterText`, `lessonOutline`, `lessonScript`, `studyDoc`, `beats`, `scene`, `segment`, `review`, `chat`). `toModelSchema()` (`shared/src/modelSchema.ts`) generates the Gemini response schemas: a scene layout is an `anyOf` with one branch per type, each with its own `required` list.
- Limits (`shared/src/limits.ts`): 140 wpm, 30 fps, `LESSON_WORDS` 420–660 and `SEGMENTS_PER_LESSON` 15–30 are prompt targets. Code clamps segment frames (6–15 s silent, up to 60 s from audio), trims extra layout items, and fits text. It does not reject or retry only because a count or length is outside the target.
- `sceneModelSchema` runs `applySegmentDefaults` first: missing `titleCard.title`, `bullets.heading`, `callout.title` become the segment title; an unknown `callout.kind` becomes `keyPoint`. Content fields are never invented.
- `packages/pipeline/src/ai_schemas.json` is a generated copy. After changing a zod schema run `npm run build -w @krayon/shared && npm run schemas -w @krayon/pipeline`; `local-backend/test/generate.test.ts` fails if it drifts.

## Error codes (`errorInfo.code`)
`errorInfo = {code, message, issues: [{path, message}], attempts}` is stored on failed segment/lesson/chapter/course docs, sent on `segment.failed` / `lesson.failed` / `chapter.failed` / `structure.failed` events, and returned by `/ask`.
| code | meaning | HTTP |
|---|---|---|
| `SCHEMA_INVALID` | JSON parsed but zod or a check rejected it after every attempt | 422 |
| `NOT_JSON` | the model output was not JSON | 422 |
| `MAX_TOKENS` | output hit the token limit (8k, or 16k for long calls) | 502 |
| `TIMEOUT` | the call was aborted (90 s, or 120 s for long calls) | 502 |
| `UPSTREAM` | any other Vertex/Gemini/TTS/transport error, or a safety block | 502 (503 if no AI backend is configured) |
| `QUOTA` | Gemini or TTS returned 429 / quota exhausted, after the backoff retries | 502 |
| `AUTH` | TTS or Gemini credentials were rejected (401/403). Not retried | 502 |
| `INVALID` | TTS rejected the request (400). Not retried | 422 |
Issue paths are relative to the validated object, e.g. `scene.layout.body: Invalid input: expected string, received undefined` or `chapters[3].pdfPageStart: Overlaps "Sorting"`.

## Logs
Location: `local-backend/logs/` (gitignored; rotated). The same lines also go to the console (the `[backend]` prefix in `npm run dev`).
- `app.log`: human-readable: `<ts> ERROR   [<request_id>] <logger>: <message> {json extras}`, stack traces inline.
- `app.jsonl`: one JSON object per line. Common keys: `ts`, `level`, `logger`, `request_id`, `msg`, `event`, `exc`.

Events (`event` key):
- `response` (`krayon.http`), one per request: `method`, `path`, `status`, `duration_ms`, redacted headers, truncated bodies. INFO for 2xx/3xx, WARNING for 4xx, ERROR for 5xx.
- `error`: an unhandled exception, with `exc`. The client gets 500 `{"detail", "requestId"}`.
- `gemini` (`krayon.gemini`): one per model call: `call_type` (the schema name, `repair` for a scene retry, or `api`), `model`, `finish_reason`, `usage{prompt,output,total,thinking_tokens}`, `queue_wait_ms`, `call_ms`, `duration_ms`, `attached_pages`, `full_document`, plus `courseId`/`chapterId`/`lessonId`/`segmentId`. Thinking budgets: scene 0, beats 0, review 256, repair 256, everything else 1024, overridable with `THINKING_BUDGET_<CALLTYPE>`.
- `tts` (`krayon` pipeline log, `event=tts`, `call_type=tts`): one per narration: `chars`, `ms`, `seconds`, `cache_hit`, `queue_wait_ms`. The audio bytes and `audioContent` are never logged. HTTP logs skip `audio/*` bodies the same way as images and PDFs (byte count only).
- Validated generation (`krayon.gemini`, `packages/pipeline/src/generate.ts`); `schema` is the call type:
  - `ai.attempt` (WARNING): one per rejected attempt: `schema`, `attempt`, `max_attempts`, `code`, `issues[]`, `raw` (first 1500 chars of model output).
  - `ai.repaired` (INFO): a later attempt passed.
  - `ai.accepted` (INFO): kept the best zod-valid value that still has check issues (scripts, beats).
  - `ai.failed` (ERROR): final failure: `code`, `attempts`, `issues[]`.
- Stage logs: `structure.ranges` (resolved ranges, `offset_method`), `structure.ready`, `chapter.text`, `chapter.coverage` (advice only, no retry), `chapter.split_range`, `chapter.lessons` (word counts), `chapter.ready`, `lesson.beats` (segments, seconds), `lesson.beats_fallback`, `lesson.long` (audio ran past 5 minutes), `segment.audio_long` (a clip was capped at 60 s), `segment.retry`, `segment.ready`, `lesson.ready`; each with `duration_ms`. Voice progress is the events `segment.voicing`, `segment.voiced`, `segment.voice_failed`.
- `render.done` / `render.failed` (with `duration_ms`), `render.wait` (DEBUG, `queue_wait_ms`).
- `segment.fix` (INFO): a review `patchedSegment` was rejected (`issues`). `segment.review` (ERROR): review stopped; the segment is kept as unreviewed unless it was a safety block.
- `segment.failed` / `lesson.failed` / `chapter.failed` / `structure.failed` (ERROR from the pipeline with `code` and `issues`; INFO from the event bus).
- `ai.chat` (`krayon.app`, WARNING): `/ask` failed: `status`, `code`.
- Pipeline events (`krayon.pipeline`), one per emitted event: `courseId`, `chapterId`, `lessonId`, `segmentId`, `ready`/`total`, `round`, `flow`, `step`, `score`, `pass`.
- `job`: `job_id`, `kind`, `status` (queued, running, done, error), `duration_ms`.
- `recover` (counts reset after a restart), `reset`, `startup`; at DEBUG only: `docstore.*`, `storage.*`, `gemini.text`, `queue.viewed`.

Every response carries an `X-Request-ID` header (send your own to choose it); the id propagates into job and pipeline logs, so one course run shares one `request_id`.

## Recipes
```bash
cd local-backend/logs
tail -f app.log                                                       # live
grep '<request_id>' app.log                                           # everything for one request / course run
jq -c 'select(.level=="ERROR" or .level=="WARNING") | {ts,request_id,msg,code,issues}' app.jsonl
jq -c 'select(.event=="ai.attempt") | {ts,schema,attempt,code,lessonId,segmentId,issues}' app.jsonl   # retries
jq -c 'select(.event=="ai.failed") | {ts,schema,code,attempts,chapterId,lessonId,segmentId,issues}' app.jsonl
jq -r 'select(.event=="ai.attempt" and .segmentId=="<id>") | .raw' app.jsonl                 # what the model sent
jq -c 'select(.event|test("failed$")) | {ts,event,chapterId,lessonId,segmentId,code,error}' app.jsonl
jq -s 'map(select(.event=="gemini")) | group_by(.call_type) | map({call_type:.[0].call_type, calls:length, prompt:(map(.usage.prompt//0)|add), output:(map(.usage.output//0)|add), thinking:(map(.usage.thinking_tokens//0)|add), avg_ms:((map(.call_ms//0)|add)/length|floor)})' app.jsonl   # tokens per call type
jq -s '{scene:(map(select(.event=="gemini" and .call_type=="scene"))|length), repair:(map(select(.event=="gemini" and .call_type=="repair"))|length), review:(map(select(.event=="gemini" and .call_type=="review"))|length), scene_check_failures:(map(select(.event=="ai.attempt" and .schema=="scene"))|length)}' app.jsonl   # scene vs repair; baseline 68 scene calls, 47 reviews. If repairs rise, set THINKING_BUDGET_SCENE=256
jq -c 'select(.event=="structure.ranges") | .ranges' app.jsonl                              # chapter page ranges
jq -r 'select(.exc) | .ts + " " + .request_id + "\n" + .exc' app.jsonl                       # stack traces
sqlite3 ../data/firestore.sqlite3 "select collection,id,json_extract(data,'$.error') from docs where json_extract(data,'$.status')='failed'"
```
In the browser: the Network tab shows `X-Request-ID` on every `/api` response; failed parts show their message with Retry where they happened (course banner, chapter header, lesson row and lesson page).

## Settings (`local-backend/.env`)
Full local list: `local-backend/.env.example`. Restart the backend after changing them.
- `LOG_LEVEL` (`INFO`; `DEBUG` adds docstore, storage and raw Gemini output), `LOG_BODY_MAX` (2000), `LOG_DIR` (`./logs`), `DATA_DIR` (`./data`), `PORT` (8787).
- `MAX_REPAIR_ROUNDS` (2): a broken scene gets `MAX_REPAIR_ROUNDS + 1` validated calls. 429s are retried with backoff inside each call; `MAX_TOKENS` fails at once.
- `MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS` (2), `REVIEW_PASS_SCORE` (8), `SEGMENT_RETRIES` (2), `CHAPTER_CONCURRENCY` (3), `GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENCY` (5), `RENDER_CONCURRENCY` (2), `RENDER_KEYFRAMES_MAX` (8), `RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS` (90000), `GEMINI_REVIEW_MODEL`.
- Caps (`CAP_*`, default 0 = off): over the cap the API returns `429 { code: 'demo_limit' }`.
- GCP worker also reads `STALE_MINUTES` (15) and `TASK_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (3); those are Cloud Run env, not local-backend config.
- TTS: `TTS_ENABLED` (true), `TTS_VOICE` (`en-US-Chirp3-HD-Charon`), `TTS_RATE` (1.0), `TTS_CONCURRENCY` (4), `TTS_QUOTA_PROJECT` (`krayon-ai`). Chirp 3 HD, LINEAR16 WAV at 24 kHz, one file per segment. A 403 usually means ADC has no quota project: `gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project krayon-ai`. Health is `GET /v1/voices` and does not gate `/api/health` `ok`. `GET /api/audio/:blobId` supports `Range`.
- `THINKING_BUDGET_<CALLTYPE>` overrides the thinking budget for one call type (`THINKING_BUDGET_SCENE`, `THINKING_BUDGET_BEATS`, `THINKING_BUDGET_REVIEW`, `THINKING_BUDGET_REPAIR`, and the same for `structure`, `chapterText`, `lessonOutline`, `lessonScript`, `studyDoc`, `chat`). Unset: scene 0, beats 0, review 256, repair 256, everything else 1024.
- To test without touching the dev server or its data, run another instance: `PORT=8797 DATA_DIR=/tmp/k/data LOG_DIR=/tmp/k/logs npx tsx src/index.ts` in `local-backend/`.

## GCP
On Cloud Run, logs are structured JSON on stdout (`backend/src/adapters/cloudLogging.ts`). Cloud Logging picks up `severity` and `logging.googleapis.com/trace` from `TRACE_HEADER`. The browser uses Firestore `onSnapshot` for realtime, not `/ws`. See `backend/architecture.md`.

## Rules for agents
- Check `app.jsonl` for the failing request id before guessing; quote the relevant lines (`ai.attempt` → `ai.failed` → `segment.failed` → `lesson.failed`).
- Never print or log secrets. The logger masks keys matching authorization, cookie, api key, token, secret, password or credential, plus `AIza…`, `ya29.…` and `Bearer …` values. A number under such a key is kept (so `usage.thinking_tokens` stays visible); a string is always masked, even a digits-only one.
- Don't reset data (`/api/admin/reset`) or delete `data/` or `logs/` unless the user asks.
